[patterns/application/micro-frontend/PTN-APP-MFE-011-shared-context-pattern.md#technical-context]

### Technical Context

**Application Architecture:**
- Shell Application: Single-SPA root config, owns global state
- Micro-Frontends: 6-10 independently loaded modules
- No shared build process or runtime except shell

**Current State (No Shared Context):**

```typescript
// ❌ PROBLEM: Each module maintains own copy of notification count

// header-mfe/src/components/NotificationBadge.tsx
function NotificationBadge() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

  useEffect(() => {
    // Fetch notification count
    fetch('/api/notifications/count').then((res) => res.json()).then(setCount);
  }, []);

  return <Badge count={count} />;
}

// notifications-mfe/src/pages/NotificationsList.tsx
function NotificationsList() {
  const [notifications, setNotifications] = useState([]);

  useEffect(() => {
    // Fetch full notification list
    fetch('/api/notifications').then((res) => res.json()).then(setNotifications);
  }, []);

  // User marks notification as read
  function markAsRead(id) {
    // Update backend
    fetch(`/api/notifications/${id}/read`, { method: 'POST' });

    // Update local state
    setNotifications((prev) => prev.map((n) => (n.id === id ? { ...n, read: true } : n)));

    // ❌ Header badge still shows old count!
    // No way to notify header-mfe about change
  }

  return <NotificationList onMarkAsRead={markAsRead} />;
}
```

**Problems:**
1. Header and Notifications panel have independent state copies
2. Marking notification as read updates panel but not header badge
3. Both modules fetch from backend independently (redundant API calls)
4. State divergence creates inconsistent UX

