[patterns/application/micro-frontend/PTN-APP-MFE-011-shared-context-pattern.md#variation-2-context-with-optimistic-updates]

#### Variation 2: Context with Optimistic Updates

Update local state immediately; rollback if backend fails (better UX).

**When to Use:**
- Marking notifications as read (instant feedback)
- Completing prior authorization reviews (no loading spinner)
- Updating claims adjudication workflow step progress (instant UI update)
- Real-time collaboration (instant UI update)

**Implementation:**

```typescript
const markAsRead = useCallback(async (id: string) => {
  // Store previous state for rollback
  const previousNotifications = notifications;

  try {
    // Optimistic update
    setNotifications((prev) =>
      prev.map((n) => (n.id === id ? { ...n, read: true } : n))
    );

    // Backend API call
    const response = await fetch(`/api/notifications/${id}/read`, {
      method: 'POST',
    });

    if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Failed to mark as read');
  } catch (error) {
    // Rollback on error
    setNotifications(previousNotifications);
    showErrorToast('Failed to mark as read');
  }
}, [notifications]);
```

**Trade-offs:**
- **Better UX**: Instant feedback (no loading spinners)
- **Complexity**: Must handle rollback logic for failures
- **Consistency Risk**: Brief period where UI shows optimistic state but backend hasn't persisted

